	dc:title	"Activation of c-Jun N-terminal kinase (JNK) and Forkhead box O (FOXO) and reduction of WNT pathways leading to reproductive failure: Integrated multi-OMICS approach for AOP building" ;
	dcterms:alternative	"JNK, FOXO and WNT alteration leading to reproductive failure: Multi-OMICS approach" ;
	dc:source	"AOPWiki" ;
	dcterms:created	"2017-02-15T04:35:06" ;
	dcterms:modified	"2023-04-29T16:02:59" ;
	dc:creator	"""Jinhee Choi, University of Seoul, Republic of Korea

Nivedita Chatterjee,&nbsp;University of Seoul, Republic of Korea

Jaeseong Jeong, University of Seoul, Republic of Korea
""" ;
	dcterms:abstract	"""Systems toxicology approach using integrated omics can provide a comprehensive insight into the mechanism of toxicity and metabolic effects when profile new chemical toxicity. The comprehensive toxic mechanism of stress response of graphene oxide was investigated in C. elegans using transcriptomics, metabolomics and lipidomics. Based on these results, we construct AOP for oxidative stress leading to reproductive failure in C. elegans. This AOP is constituted the KEs as increased oxidative stress and activation of c-Jun N-terminal kinase (JNK) and the activation of transcription factor DAF-16/FOXO, inhibition of WNT signaling, defect embryogenesis and AO as reproductive failure.
""" ;
	dcterms:license	<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/> ;
