	dc:creator	"""Laure-Alix Clerbaux, Julija Filipovska, Amalia Munoz-Pineiro, Lucia Grenga
""" ;
	dcterms:abstract	"""S-protein binding to ACE2  receptor induces dysregulation of  ACE2 physiological functions in the intestines such as modulation of the local renin-angiotensin signaling (RAS) system (10.1152/ajpgi.00099.202) or as a chaperone for dietary amino acid (AA) transporters in the intestines, such as the tryptophan transporter B0AT1 (Slc6a19) (10.1042/CS20200477; 10.1053/j.gastro.2008.10.055). The gastrointestinal RAS appears to be involved in numerous processes in the gut including AA, fluid and electrolyte absorption and secretion (10.1111/j.1365-2036.2011.04971.x.). Besides, the gut microbiota is influenced by the host intestinal AA metabolism as gut bacteria use dietary AA for protein synthesis (10.1038/s41598-020-74122-9). 
""" ;
