""" ;
	aopo:has_evidence	"""The QWOE approach is an analytical method that utilizes causality criteria to assess the evidence-supported postulated AOP[4]. Firstly, the hypothesis of action was presented and the quantitative&nbsp;evaluation of evidence ranging from no evidence (0) to strong for each category (3, strong and &minus;3, strong counter) utilizing the evolved MIEs, KEs, and KERs. Subsequently, a ranked importance-based numerical weight was assigned to Bradford Hill causal considerations, and the composite&nbsp;score and confidence score for MIEs, KEs, and entire AOP were evaluated. 


	
		
