aop:540
	a	aopo:AdverseOutcomePathway ;
	dc:identifier	aop:540 ;
	rdfs:label	"AOP 540" ;
	rdfs:seeAlso	<https://identifiers.org/aop/540> ;
	foaf:page	<https://identifiers.org/aop/540> ;
	dc:title	"Oxidative Stress in the Fish Ovary Leads to Reproductive Impairment via Reduced Vitellogenin Production" ;
	dcterms:alternative	"ROS in Fish Ovary Impairs Reproduction" ;
	dc:source	"AOPWiki" ;
	dcterms:created	"2024-07-19T10:53:04" ;
	dcterms:modified	"2024-10-16T09:30:39" ;
	dc:description	"""Contaminant induced generation of excess ROS and subsequent&nbsp;oxidative stress has been measured in fish ovaries after exposure to mutliple different classes of toxicants including pesticides, metals, plasticizers, and nanoplastics. Effects on fish reproductive fecundity has also been demonstrated for these stressors either concurrently or in independent studies. This AOP provides linkage between increased oxidative stress and adverse outcomes related to reduced fecundity in fish which is known to significantly effect fish population demographics.
""", """Maintenance of sustainable fish and wildlife populations (i.e., adequate to ensure long-term delivery of valued ecosystem services) is a widely accepted regulatory goal upon which risk assessments and risk management decisions are based.
""" ;
	dc:creator	"""Kevin V. Brix

EcoTox LLC

Miami, Florida

KevinBrix@EcoTox.onmicrosoft.com
""" ;
	dcterms:abstract	"""This AOP describes&nbsp;the linkage between excess reactive oxygen species (ROS) in the fish ovary and reductions in fish fecundity&nbsp;leading to population level impacts. The AOP largely relies on key events (KEs) and key event relationships (KERs) that have been previously described in other AOPs linking&nbsp;reduction in estradiol (E2) synthesis&nbsp;to decreased population growth rates. The novel aspect of this AOP is the development of evidence supporting excess ROS and corresponding oxidative stress in the fish ovary as another molecular initiating event (MIE) and initial KE that can lead to initiation of this pathway.
""" ;
	dcterms:license	<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/> ;
	aopo:has_key_event	aop.events:1392, aop.events:1262, aop.events:3, aop.events:285, aop.events:221, aop.events:309, aop.events:78, aop.events:1115, aop.events:360 ;
	aopo:has_key_event_relationship	aop.relationships:2009, aop.relationships:3326, aop.relationships:3249, aop.relationships:3327, aop.relationships:315, aop.relationships:255, aop.relationships:337, aop.relationships:94 ;
	aopo:has_molecular_initiating_event	aop.events:1115 ;
	aopo:has_adverse_outcome	aop.events:360 ;
	pato:0000047	"Female" .

