	dc:title	"Activation, Hepatic nuclear receptor(s)" ;
	dcterms:alternative	"Activation, Hepatic nuclear receptor(s)" ;
	dc:source	"AOPWiki" ;
	nci:C25664	"""Molecular""" ;
	nci:C17469	"""Taxonomic:&nbsp;Based on Noyes et al., 2019, constitutive androstane receptor (CAR) activation, aryl hydrocarbon receptor (AhR) activation, and peroxisome proliferator-activated receptors (PPAR&alpha;/&gamma;/&delta;) activation were considered as the hepatic nuclear receptor(s) within this MIE to perform a specific taxonomic domain of applicability (tDOA) assessment by Haigis et al. (2023). The authors found structural protein conservation of mammalian and amphibian CAR compared to the human (Homo sapiens) protein target using the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency&rsquo;s Sequence Alignment to Predict Across Species Susceptibility (SeqAPASS v6.0; seqapass.epa.gov/seqapass/) tool, while acknowledging the potential existence of interspecies differences in conservation. This conservation was not found in fish, birds or reptiles. Using the SeqAPASS tool, structural protein conservation of mammalian, amphibian, fish, reptilian and avian AhR and the PPARs (PPAR&alpha;, &gamma;, &delta;) was found compared to the human sequence.
""" ;
	aopo:CellTypeContext	cl:0000182 ;
	aopo:hasBiologicalEvent	<1157_bioevent_0> ;
	go:0008150	go:0023052 ;
	pato:0000001	"increased" ;
	pato:0001241	pr:000000001 ;
	dcterms:isPartOf	aop:194 .

