	dc:source	"AOPWiki" ;
	dc:description	"""Heart failure, also known as cardiac arrest,&nbsp;refers to the heart ceasing to pump blood through the circulatory system.
""" ;
	mmo:0000000	"""Heart failure can be measured by electrocardiograms to assess heart electrical activity across a wide variety of animal taxa to determine&nbsp;when heart rate falls to zero (Hauser et al. 2012).
""" ;
	nci:C25664	"""Organ""" ;
	nci:C17469	"""Life Stage: Applies to all life stages with developed heart; not specific to any life stage.


Sex: Applies to both males and females; not sex-specific.


