	dc:description	"""Taxa = necrotic tissue in the liver

During the process of towards necrotic tissue, too many cells die. In practice it is difficult to distinguish separate forms of cell death (apoptosis, necrosis and necroptosis), especially in vivo.
""" ;
	mmo:0000000	"""Histopathology: performed on tissue sections

&middot; Hematoxylin (nuclei) and eosin staining: determine morphology

&middot; TUNEL staining: cell death

https://medical-dictionary.thefreedictionary.com/Necrotic+tissue

