	dc:title	"Interaction of α-diketones with arginine residues" ;
	dcterms:alternative	"Interaction of α-diketones with arginine residues" ;
	dc:source	"AOPWiki" ;
	dc:description	"""The electrophilic &alpha;-diketones interact with proteins via direct covalent binding to cellular nucleophiles. The interaction occurs predominantly with the arginine residues of proteins.
""" ;
	mmo:0000000	"""The binding of &alpha;-diketones with proteins can be measured by LC-MS and 1H- and 13C NMR analysis (Anders 2017, Mathews et al. 2010, Saraiva et al. 2016)
""" ;
	nci:C25664	"""Molecular""" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf	aop:280 .

aop.events:1585
	a	aopo:KeyEvent ;
	dc:identifier	aop.events:1585 ;
	rdfs:label	"KE 1585" ;
	foaf:page	<https://identifiers.org/aop.events/1585> ;
	rdfs:seeAlso	<https://identifiers.org/aop.events/1585> ;
	dc:title	"Proteasomal dysfunction" ;
	dcterms:alternative	"Proteasomal dysfunction" ;
	dc:source	"AOPWiki" ;
	dc:description	"""The covalent interaction of &alpha;-diketones with arginines leads to altered structure and functioning of proteins. Indication of widespread protein damage was observed in DA exposed mice (Hubbs et al. 2016)
""" ;
	mmo:0000000	"""The inactivation of enzymes due to the interaction of &alpha;-diketones with arginine residues at their active sites has been demonstrated (Chen and Chen 2003). Protein damage has been measured by accumulation of ubiquitin and sequestosome-1 in the lungs of exposed mice (Hubbs et al. 2016)
""" ;
	nci:C25664	"""Molecular""" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf	aop:280, aop:464 .

aop.events:1586
	a	aopo:KeyEvent ;
	dc:identifier	aop.events:1586 ;
	rdfs:label	"KE 1586" ;
	foaf:page	<https://identifiers.org/aop.events/1586> ;
	rdfs:seeAlso	<https://identifiers.org/aop.events/1586> ;
	dc:title	"Airway epithelial injury" ;
	dcterms:alternative	"Airway epithelial injury" ;
	dc:source	"AOPWiki" ;
	dc:description	"""Inhalation of to low concentrations of &alpha;-diketones generally does not result in airway injury. However, above a certain threshold the airway epithelium becomes persistently damaged.
""" ;
	mmo:0000000	"""Histopathological abnormalities in exposed rats, airway epithelial necrosis, flattening of the airway epithelial cells, loss of cilia (Foster et al. 2017), gaps in the epithelial layer (Hubbs et al. 2002, 2008). Also a reduced expression of club cell secretory protein in airway epithelium has been observed after a-diketone exposure (Palmer et al. 2011). Within in vitro models of airway epithelium, the loss of epithelial barrier function following exposure can be measured as a reduction in transepithelial electrical resistance (TEER, Fedan et al. 2006, Zaccone et al 2015)
""" ;
	nci:C25664	"""Cellular""" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf	aop:280, aop:481 .

aop.events:1587
	a	aopo:KeyEvent ;
	dc:identifier	aop.events:1587 ;
	rdfs:label	"KE 1587" ;
	foaf:page	<https://identifiers.org/aop.events/1587> ;
	rdfs:seeAlso	<https://identifiers.org/aop.events/1587> ;
	dc:title	"Fibroproliferative airway lesions" ;
	dcterms:alternative	"Fibroproliferative airway lesions" ;
	dc:source	"AOPWiki" ;
	dc:description	"""Repeated exposure to &alpha;-diketones might result in the loss of the regenerative capacity of the airway epithelium, e.g. due to insufficient residual stem cells. Sustained loss of the epithelial cells might lead to damage to the underlying basement membrane and exposure of the lamina propria. Fibroblast in the lamina propria are activated and start to proliferate and elaborate collagen matrix. Cytokines and growth factors released by epithelial cells and infiltrated neutrophils may promote the migration and proliferation of fibroblasts into the airway lumen. The initially fibromyxoid tissue is gradually replaced by mature connective tissue that is rich in collagen (rats, Flake &amp; Morgan 2017).
""" ;
	mmo:0000000	"""Fibroproliferative airway lesions can be observed in biopsies of &alpha;-diketone exposed laboratory animals in a dose dependent manner using various tissue stainings of histological specimen. (rats, Morgan et al. 2016, Flake &amp; Morgan 2017)
""" ;
	nci:C25664	"""Tissue""" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf	aop:280 .

aop.events:1588
	a	aopo:KeyEvent ;
	dc:identifier	aop.events:1588 ;
	rdfs:label	"KE 1588" ;
