	dc:description	"""Lipid peroxidation of membrane lipids has been considered to be one of the major mechanisms in phototoxic skin responses induced by photoreactive chemicals&nbsp;(Castell et al., 1994, Girotti, 1990, 2001, Onoue et al., 2011, Onoue and Tsuda, 2006, Seto et al., 2013).
""" ;
	mmo:0000000	"""An in vitro system using thiobarbituric acid can monitor lipid peroxidation by photoactivated chemicals  ADDIN EN.CITE  ADDIN EN.CITE.DATA 
 
(Onoue et al., 2011, Onoue and Tsuda, 2006)
 
.
""" ;
	nci:C25664	"""Cellular""" ;
	nci:C17469	"""Chemicals: This KE applies to a wide range of chemicals.&nbsp; The chemicals generate a reactive species, such as reactive oxygen species, following absorption of photon energy from light within the range of natural sunlight (290-700 nm) (ICH, 2014, Onoue and Tsuda, 2006).



Sex: This KE applies to both males and females.&nbsp;

Life stages: The relevant life stages for this KE are all life stages after born.

Taxonomic: This KE mainly applies to human. 
""" ;
