	nci:C17469	"""Hyperinflammation is observed in all age groups with high rates of infection and mortality observed in aged population. In children, although the rate of infection is low, hyperinflammatory syndrome is observed leading to long term disabilities. However, mortality rate in young children and adults below 40 years of age is less pronounced. Data in other developmental stages is lacking.

Prevalence of hyperinflammation is same in men and women; however, studies have found that men develop more severe symptoms than women.
""" ;
