	aopo:has_upstream_key_event	aop.events:227 ;
	aopo:has_downstream_key_event	aop.events:1170 ;
	dc:description	"""Activation of the PPAR&alpha; receptor leads to a coordinated gene expression program that produces lipid metabolizing enzymes and proteins associated with control of the cell cycle.
""" ;
	nci:C80263	"""Similar to other nuclear receptors such as the aryl hydrocarbon receptor (AHR) and constitutive androstane receptor (CAR), PPAR&alpha; induces a coordinated gene expression program (Corton et al. 2014; Elcombe et al. 2014; Budinsky et al. 2014).
""" ;
	edam:data_2042	"""Alteration of genes/proteins involved in cell growth by PPAR&alpha; activators was not observed in PPAR&alpha;-null mice (Anderson et al. 2004; Belury et al. 1998; Corton et al. 2004, 2014; Cunningham et al. 2010; Fitzgerald et al. 1981; Hartig et al. 1982; NTP, 2007)
""" ;
	nci:C71478	"""Vanishingly few, if any.
""" ;
	nci:C68821	"""Modulating factors include NF-kB activation, cytokines, oxidative stress, and the role of microRNAs.
""" ;
	nci:C17469	"""The domain of applicability is similar to that for the overall MIE.
""" ;
	edam:operation_3799	"""The activities for acyl coenzyme A oxidase for the three stressors considered on the main page of this AOP (AOP 37) were plotted and fit to a hockey stick dose-response model (Lutz &amp; Lutz, 2009) and shown below.



&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The central value for the threshold MIE level was 14.15 MIE units with&nbsp;confidence limits of 3.04&nbsp;to 19.07. &nbsp;
""" ;
	edam:operation_3438	"""The enzyme response does not occur until at least 14 MIE units and then rises with a slope of 0.72 per MIE unit.
""" ;
	nci:C25207	"""The time scale of both the MIE and the enzyme response is 1 week.
""" ;
	nci:C25343	"""Increased expression of ACO and associated oxidative stress activated NF-kB
""" ;
	pato:0000047	"Mixed" ;
	aopo:LifeStageContext	"All life stages" ;
	ncbitaxon:131567	ncbitaxon:10090, ncbitaxon:10116 ;
	dcterms:isPartOf	aop:37 .

aop.relationships:1230
	a	aopo:KeyEventRelationship ;
	dc:identifier	aop.relationships:1230 ;
	rdfs:label	"KER 1230" ;
	foaf:page	<https://identifiers.org/aop.relationships/1230> ;
	rdfs:seeAlso	<https://identifiers.org/aop.relationships/1230> ;
	dcterms:created	"2016-11-29T18:41:37" ;
	dcterms:modified	"2020-12-31T13:00:17" ;
	aopo:has_upstream_key_event	aop.events:1170 ;
	aopo:has_downstream_key_event	aop.events:716 ;
	dc:description	"""Growth factors and other cytokines&nbsp;secreted from Kupffer cells following PPAR&alpha; activation include&nbsp;tumor necrosis factor &alpha; (TNF&alpha;), interleukin-1&alpha; (IL-1&alpha;), and interleukin-1&beta; (IL-1&beta;). Although TNF&alpha; levels increase following PPAR&alpha; activation, proliferation was observed in wild type, TNF&alpha;-null, and&nbsp;TNF&alpha; receptor-null mice, suggesting that multiple cytokines stimulate cell proliferation (Maeda et al. 2005). PPAR&alpha; activation reduces the level of miRNA let-7c in liver. In turn, let-7c normally down-regulates c-Myc expression and thus,&nbsp;PPAR&alpha; activation increases c-Myc expression that increase cell proliferation (Shah et al. 2007).&nbsp;PPAR&alpha; activation increases levels of other cell cycle proteins&nbsp;including&nbsp;Cdk-1, Cdk-4, Cyclin D1&nbsp;and&nbsp;Pcna&nbsp;(Currie et al. 2005; Woods et al. 2007).

&nbsp;
""" ;
	nci:C80263	"""Whilst knowledge of the molecular pathways underlying cell proliferation remains incomplete, the consistent observation of increases in both cell proliferation, liver weight and cytokine levels are consistent with biological knowledge.
""" ;
	edam:data_2042	"""Alteration of genes/proteins involved in cell growth by PPAR&alpha; activators was not observed in PPAR&alpha;-null mice
""" ;
	nci:C71478	"""The precise mechanism for activation of growth control genes is not known.&nbsp;
""" ;
	nci:C17469	"""The domain of applicability is the same as for AOP 37.
""" ;
	edam:operation_3799	"""Cell proliferation measured by BrdU labeling index was plotted against the&nbsp;enzyme response of the three&nbsp;PPAR&alpha; activators. The enzyme measured was acyl CoA oxidase, a lipid-metabolizing enzyme and was considered a surrogate for the cytokines and other growth-related cytokines stimulated by&nbsp;PPAR&alpha; activation. These data were well fit by a Michaelis-Menten equation, suggesting that receptor mechanisms are likely involved in the growth response.



&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The&nbsp;

The maximal proliferation level was 30.88% and the half-maximal enzyme response was 3.37.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;
""" ;
	edam:operation_3438	"""Levels of cytokines and other cellular proteins involved in cell cycle control are increased concomitant with increased enzyme activity and stimulate cell proliferation.&nbsp;
""" ;
	nci:C25207	"""Both responses considered above occured 1 week after commencing&nbsp;PPAR&alpha; activation.
""" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf	aop:37 .

