aop.relationships:1962
	a	aopo:KeyEventRelationship ;
	dc:identifier	aop.relationships:1962 ;
	rdfs:label	"KER 1962" ;
	foaf:page	<https://identifiers.org/aop.relationships/1962> ;
	rdfs:seeAlso	<https://identifiers.org/aop.relationships/1962> ;
	dcterms:created	"2019-07-03T11:52:25" ;
	dcterms:modified	"2019-08-13T05:25:46" ;
	aopo:has_upstream_key_event	aop.events:1668 ;
	aopo:has_downstream_key_event	aop.events:87 ;
	dc:description	"""Phagocytosis allow the clearance of foreign matter. Incomplete phagocytosis, or frustrated phagocytosis, leads to the persistence of foreign matter. Therefore, in order to clear these substances, phagocytes secretes signals including cytokines for the recruitment of other phagocytes.
""" ;
	nci:C80263	"""The main function of professional phagocytes is to clear the tissue of the foreign matter by phagocytosis [1]. Following exposure to foreign matter, macrophages are activated and therefore secrete pro-inflammatory mediators including cytokines [1].
""" ;
	edam:data_2042	"""In the study of Murphy et al, the human monocytic THP-1 cells treated with carbon nanotubes (CNTs) that induce frustrated phagocytosis showed an increase production of IL-1&beta;, IL-6 and IL-8 whereas treatment by CNTs that did not induce this process did not induce production of these cytokines [2]. Similarly, it was shown that exposure to fibres that induced frustrated phagocytosis of primary human alveolar macrophages is accompanied by induction of IL-6 and IL-8 [3], and exposure of immortalized MH-S murine alveolar macrophage is accompanied by induction of TNF&alpha; and IL-1&alpha; [4, 5]. The induction of cytokines was observed in lesser extend after cell treatment with fibres that did not cause frustrated phagocytosis. Indeed, the ratio of the dose-response for TNF&alpha; and IL-1&alpha; of long fibres to short fibres was about 11 [4, 5].
""" ;
	nci:C71478	"""In very few studies it was analysed the release of cytokines in the same samples as the frustrated phagocytosis.

A study of Zeidler-Erdely et al 2006 showed that human alveolar macrophages are able to engulf fibres with a length of 20 &micro;m and explained this difference with rat alveolar macrophages are smaller than human cells [6]. However, these data are not in accordance with those obtained by Sweeney et al 2015 were they used primary human alveolar macrophages&nbsp; and by Murphy et al 2012 were they used monocytic cells THP-1 differentiated in macrophages [2, 3]. 
""" ;
	edam:operation_3438	"""The length of fibres that induced frustrated phagocytosis accompanied by cytokines production were comprised between 13 and 39.3 &micro;m, whereas fibres with length between 1 and 7 &micro;m were completely phagocytosed and did not induce cytokine production [2, 3, 4].
""" ;
	nci:C25207	"""The frustrated phagocytosis and cytokine production were observed after 16 to 24h of treatment [2, 3, 4, 5].
""" ;
	pato:0000047	"Unspecific" ;
	aopo:LifeStageContext	"Adult" ;
	ncbitaxon:131567	"WikiUser_17" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf	aop:303 .

