			1 &micro;M
			
			
			48 h or

			72 h
			
			
			Ectopic expression of meiotic markers (Stra8, Sycp3, Dmc1) and decrease in pluripotency marker Oct4
			
			
			(Bowles et al, 2006)
			
		
		
			
			Fetal testes in culture
			
			
			Mouse
			
			
			Ketoconazole (Cyp26 inhibitor)
			
			
			40 &micro;M
			
			
			48 h or

			72 h
			
			
			Ectopic expression of meiotic markers (Stra8, Sycp3, Dmc1) and decrease in pluripotency marker Oct4
			
			
			(Bowles et al, 2006)
			
		
		
			
			Fetal testes in culture
			
			
			Mouse
			
			
			BMS-194753

			(RAR-&alpha; agonist)
			
			
			0.5 &micro;M
			
			
			2 d
			
			
			Ectopic Stra8 expression 
			
			
			(Koubova et al, 2006)
			
		
		
			
			Fetal testes in culture
			
			
			Mouse
			
			
			BMS-213309

			(RAR-&beta; agonist)
			
			
			0.5 &micro;M
			
			
			2 d
			
			
			Ectopic Stra8 expression
			
			
			(Koubova et al, 2006)
			
		
		
			
			Fetal testes in culture
			
			
			Mouse
			
			
			BMS-270394

			(RAR-&gamma; agonist)
			
			
			0.5 &micro;M
			
			
			2 d
			
			
			Ectopic Stra8 expression
			
			
			(Koubova et al, 2006)
			
		
		
			
			Fetal testes in culture
			
			
			Mouse
			
			
			atRA
			
			
			0.7 &micro;M
			
			
			2 d
			
			
			Ectopic Stra8 expression
			
			
			(Koubova et al, 2006)
			
		
		
			
			Fetal testes in culture
			
			
			Mouse
			
			
			Ketoconazole

			(Cyp26 inhibitor)
			
			
			0.7 &micro;M
			
			
			2 d
			
			
			Ectopic Stra8 expression
			
			
			(Koubova et al, 2006)
			
		
		
			
			Fetal testes in culture
			
			
			Mouse
			
			
			R115866

			(Cyp26 inhibitor)
			
			
			0.7 &micro;M
			
			
			2 d
			
			
			Ectopic Stra8 expression
			
			
			(Koubova et al, 2006)
			
		
		
			
			Fetal testes in culture
			
			
			Rats
			
			
			atRA
			
			
			1 &micro;M and 0.031 &micro;M 
			
			
			2 or 3 d
			
			
			Increased apoptosis of germ cells, reduction in total number of germ cells
			
			
			(Livera et al, 2000a)
			
		
		
			
			Culture of fetal testis single cell suspension 
			
			
			Human
			
			
			atRA
			
			
			1 &micro;M
			
			
			24 h
			
			
			Increased STRA8 expression, but had no effect on DMC1 or SYCP3 expression
			
			
			(Childs et al, 2011)
			
		
	


&nbsp;

&nbsp;
""" ;
	nci:C71478	"""Mouse deletion model for the atRA synthesis enzymes Aldh1a1, Aldh1a2 and Aldh1a3 showed decreased expression of&nbsp; Stra8 in double (Aldh1a2/3) and triple (Aldh1a1/2/3) knockouts, although ultimately germ cells were observed undergoing meiosis in these ovaries, suggesting redundant role for atRA (Chassot et al, 2020; Kumar et al, 2011). Similarly, transgenic mice lacking the three atRA nuclear receptors (RAR-a, -b, -g) showed reduced levels of Stra8, although ultimately germ cells were observed undergoing meiosis and were capable of producing live offspring (Vernet et al, 2020). Whether or not these models led to impaired fertility (such as sub-fertility) has not been elucidated and the size of their oocyte pools were not determined.

Gain of function mouse ovary models for CYP26A1 and CYP26B1 shows that CYP26B1 can prevent oocytes from entering meiosis (as in, failure to induce Stra8 expression), whereas CYP26A1 does not have the same effect despite being a potent atRA degrading enzyme. This suggests that factor(s) in addition to atRA are required for meiosis induction (Bellutti et al, 2019).
""" ;
	edam:operation_3799	"""There is a very limited quantitative understanding of this KER other than the knowledge that when germ cells, from either testis or ovary, are cultured in the presence of atRA, at concentrations as low as 10nM, Stra8 expression is rapidly induced (Spiller &amp; Bowles, 2019).
""" ;
	edam:operation_3438	"""In vitro and ex vivo, it has been conclusively shown that low levels of exogenous atRA can induce germ cells to enter meiosis in mice (Bowles et al, 2006) and rats (Livera et al, 2000b) and, similarly, that it is necessary to achieve meiosis in in-vitro-derived oocytes via PGCLCs (Miyauchi et al, 2017). Yet, its exact role in vivo is debated. 

Whilst the relative levels of endogenous atRA produced by the ovary (for any species) remains unknown, similarly, the quantitative relationship between atRA levels and induction of meiosis also remains unclear. As such, the quantitative understanding of how much atRA needs to be reduced to prevent germ cells from entering meiosis in vivo is rated low.
""" ;
	pato:0000047	"Male" ;
	aopo:LifeStageContext	"Fetal" ;
	ncbitaxon:131567	ncbitaxon:10090, ncbitaxon:10116, "WCS_9606" ;
	dcterms:isPartOf	aop:400 .

